\begin{example}
\label{ex:real-projective-plane-elliptic-geometry}
\uses{ex:real-projective-space-metric, prop:rp-n-frame-homogeneous, prob:rp-n-frame-homogeneous, prob:elliptic-geometry-hilbert}
\dcref{ch5:5.30}

The real projective plane $\mathbb{RP}^2$ carries a frame-homogeneous metric
$g$ locally isometric to a round metric on $S^n$ by Example 2.34 and
\cref{prop:rp-n-frame-homogeneous}. With points given by elements of
$\mathbb{RP}^2$ and lines by
images of maximal geodesics, the incidence postulates and the elliptic parallel
postulate hold. This is \emph{single elliptic geometry}.
\end{example}

